  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1974-p22.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let \\(u=\\frac{A}{2}.\\) Then \\(\\sin u-\\sqrt3\\cos u\\) equals \\(2\\sin(u-60^\\circ).\\) Its minimum occurs when \\(u-60^\\circ=270^\\circ+360^\\circ n,\\) so \\[ A=660^\\circ+720^\\circ n \\] for an integer \\(n.\\) None of the first four choices has this form.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Combine the sine and cosine into one shifted sine with amplitude \\(2\\)",
        "Use \\(\\sin u-\\sqrt3\\cos u=2\\sin(u-60^\\circ)\\)"
      ],
